#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0114 expect=noViolation domain=CO
#note "THE COVAL1/COVAL2 PIN (Fix #294 / M3-D15(iii)). Two comments that are DIFFERENT but whose first 200-character section (COVAL) is IDENTICAL, split across COVAL/COVAL1 as CDISC-SEND-0095/0095.1 require: they differ only in COVAL1. Before M3-D15 the identity tuple named COVAL alone, so the two rows shared the whole key and were reported as duplicates -- an over-report on exactly the mechanism the family elsewhere enforces. With COVAL1 and COVAL2 in the tuple they are distinct and the rule is silent. Absent members are dropped at runtime, so no dataset that does not split comments is affected."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset CO
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col POOLID   type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col COSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col COVAL    type=Char label="Comment"
col COVAL1   type=Char label="Comment Part 1"
col COVAL2   type=Char label="Comment Part 2"
col CODTC    type=Char label="Date/Time of Comment"
---
STUDY01 | CO | BW | 001 |  | BWSEQ | 1 | 1 | SAMEFIRSTSECTION | FIRSTTAIL  |  | 2023-01-15
STUDY01 | CO | BW | 001 |  | BWSEQ | 1 | 2 | SAMEFIRSTSECTION | SECONDTAIL |  | 2023-01-15
---
